# Jupytext sync artifacts.
#
# Notebooks here are authored as jupytext markdown: the .md is the source of
# truth, it is what test/notebooks/test_notebooks.py executes in CI, and it
# carries no saved outputs, so it diffs and reviews like code. Editing one in
# JupyterLab or VS Code produces a paired .ipynb beside it — that file is a
# local working copy, and committing it would put a second, divergent version
# of the same document in the repo along with megabytes of embedded output.
#
# The four .ipynb already tracked here predate the convention. Gitignore does
# not affect tracked files, so they are unaffected; adding a genuinely new
# .ipynb needs `git add -f` and a moment's thought about whether it should be
# markdown instead.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_*
